  "question": {
    "text": "The ground state energy of hydrogen atom is <math><mo>-</mo><mn>13.6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> . Consider an electronic state <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#936;</mi></math> of <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> whose energy, azimuthal quantum number and magnetic quantum number are <math><mo>-</mo><mn>3.4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mn>0</mn></math> respectively. Which of the following statement(s) is(are) true for the state <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#936;</mi></math> ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "qp2LT",
      "text": "It has <math><mn>2</mn></math> angular nodes",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uyMmF",
      "text": "It has <math><mn>3</mn></math> radial nodes",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "rBHEA",
      "text": "It is a <math><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> state",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0UR4u",
      "text": "The nuclear charge experienced by the electron in this state is less than <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math> , where e is the magnitude of the electronic charge.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mo>∵</mo><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13.6</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13.6</mn><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3.4</mn></math>  <br/><math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>  <br/><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>  <br/><math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> belongs to <math><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></math> orbital <br/><math><mo>→</mo></math> Radial nodes <math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>  <br/><math><mo>→</mo></math> Angular nodes <math><mo>⇒</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>  <br/><math><mo>→</mo></math> Angular nodes <math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn></math>  <br/>Since <math><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is a single <math><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> ion, its nuclear charge experienced.",
